nge while helping residents preserve their heritage.", "encoded_message": "Large-market tourism can bring compensation and jobs, but the approach perhaps can too restructure area-based cultural legacies. Longstanding ceremonies come to resemble showcases meant for touring guests, where upward-trending lease costs and overpopulated main roads hamper daily routine existence. Cities may revoke commandership relating to consecrated places. Respectful travel supports cultural exchange while helping residents preserve their heritage.", "encoding_time_report": {"container_generation": 4.78, "secret_key_generation": 24.8}, "encoding_usage_report": {"container_generation": {"completion_tokens": 434, "prompt_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 543, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 371, "audio_tokens": 0, "accepted_prediction_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": 0}}, "secret_key_generation": {"completion_tokens": 14514, "prompt_tokens": 3062, "total_tokens": 17576}}, "decoding_time": 0.0006091594696044922, "decoded_message": "11001100001011111001001110010011101111110010000101111100110110110011111001101010000111000001100001110011001100010001100101000011", "error_message": ""}